 # Message
 
-`FixMsg` is a market event with a FIX body around it: the [event](../graph/event.md) the message is, the standard header typed, what the line's own bridge row header said about the capture it was written for, the free text and a bridge's namespaced keys - each held once, as a typed fact - and the content row, every other field the message states, typed by the registry's field for it. One message is one frame, one bridge row or one document - never the line, which can carry [several of them or none](decode.md#a-line-yields-none-one-or-many-messages).
+`FixMsg` is the FIX codec's handle over a [market message](../graph/market-data.md#the-market-message): the message - every fact it states, typed and held once, its record of every other field it states, typed by the registry's field for it, and the anomalies its reading noted - beside the standard header typed, what the line's own bridge row header said about the capture it was written for, and the indexes the codec reads the record by. `into_message` lets go of the handle and `from_message` takes a message back into it ([below](#the-market-message)). One message is one frame, one bridge row or one document - never the line, which can carry [several of them or none](decode.md#a-line-yields-none-one-or-many-messages).
 
