+## The market message
+
+`FixMsg` is a handle: the [market message](../graph/market-data.md#the-market-message) it holds is the one every protocol lands in, and what the codec keeps beside it - the header, the capture, the indexes it reads the record by - is the codec's alone. The message moves out and comes back without a text parse, and a message no FIX parse built takes the same door in.
+
+| item | contract |
+| --- | --- |
+| `into_message(self) -> MarketMessage` | lets go of the handle and moves the message out as it stands - its facts, its record, its anomalies, what it states of its instrument - the codec's word on what the source stated published as its [`StatedFacts`](../graph/market-data.md#stated-facts). What FIX alone can read off the message is read once into what the message holds, so the market side splits it by its facts alone: a direct order, quote or execution states on its metadata what no typed column reads, the identifiers among it lifted into their sets; a `W` or `X` states one child per `NoMDEntries(268)` occurrence - its record the occurrence under the group's one shared root - and its record's `NoMDEntries(268)` cell is null where the children hold them; an acknowledgement of an execution is marked one. An order or a quote every field of which a typed column reads moves without allocating |
+| `from_message(registry, message) -> Result<FixMsg>` | the way back, and the door a message no FIX parse built takes in. The codec's own record - a root holding the `BeginString(8)` every parse writes - is adopted as it is: its root shared, its indexes rebuilt once over its children, the header and the capture read off its cells, no text parsed; the children go back into its `NoMDEntries(268)` cell in their order, and the metadata loses what `into_message` rendered off the record. Any other record is laid out anew under the registry: `BeginString(8)` at the default version, `MsgType(35)` from the category where no entry states it - `8` an order or an execution, `S` a quote, `W` a book, `AE` a trade, the state riding its crate tag - every stated fact under the one standard tag the enrichment reads it from (the table below), else under its crate tag, each entry under the field the registry resolves its name to, typed through it, and an entry it resolves none for into the metadata as the text it spells. The facts are the message's, untouched - its identity included. Refused where a field's type refuses an entry |
+| The idmap rule | a tag the dictionary's [`FIX:idmap`](registry.md#a-field-names-a-message-by-its-identifiers) or its enrichment maps onto a fact - `Side(54)`, `Price(44)`, `OrderQty(38)`, every one of them - is that fact: read into it at parse, written from it on the wire and in the [fixed row](#a-row-is-a-message-again). A message's entries are the tags no fact consumes, so a side stated on the market message is the side the wire says |
+| `FixCodec::render(message) -> Result<Vec<u8>>` | `from_message`, then the wire separated by `SOH` - its `Text(58)` stated after the lifted band - with the crate's own tag of each fact no field of the frame states - the category, the state, the chain, the sources, the instant and the clocks the message holds - before the trailer. A parse of the frame restates the message: `codec.parse_fix_line(&codec.render(m)?)?.into_message()` states the facts, the stated bits, the entries, the metadata and the children `m` states, beside what the dictionary's derivations fill - a day order on an `8` - which states nothing the source stated. Rust only |
+
+| Fact | Written under |
+| --- | --- |
+| `side` | `Side(54)`, its wire character |
+| `price`, `stoppx`, `strikepx` | `Price(44)`, `StopPx(99)`, `StrikePrice(202)` |
+| `quantity`, `ordqty`, `displayqty`, `cxlqty` | `Quantity(53)`, `OrderQty(38)`, `DisplayQty(1138)`, `CxlQty(84)` |
+| `currency`, `cficode`, `unit` | `Currency(15)`, `CFICode(461)`, `UnitOfMeasure(996)` |
+| `timeinforce` | `TimeInForce(59)`, its wire value |
+| `prevpx` | `PrevClosePx(140)` |
+| `lastpx`, `spotrate`, `forwardpoints` | `LastPx(31)`, `LastSpotRate(194)`, `LastForwardPoints(195)` |
+| `lastqty`, `avgpx`, `cumqty`, `leavesqty` | `LastQty(32)`, `AvgPx(6)`, `CumQty(14)`, `LeavesQty(151)` |
+| `bidpx`, `bidqty`, `askpx`, `askqty` | `BidPx(132)`, `BidSize(134)`, `OfferPx(133)`, `OfferSize(135)` |
+| `ticker`, `miccode` | `Symbol(55)`, `LastMkt(30)` |
+| `exprunix` | `ExpireTime(126)` |
+| every other stated fact | its [crate tag](capture.md#the-crates-own-columns), 65001 to 65052 |
