+## The market message
+
+`MarketMessage`, in `graph::message`, is the one message every protocol lands in and the one `MarketData` holds whole: its facts, typed, beside what it states beyond them. A codec fills one at parse - [FIX](../fix/message.md#the-market-message) moves its own out of the handle it reads it by - and every reading past it, a walk, a merge, the leaves it splits into, reads facts alone.
+
+| Key | Rule |
+| --- | --- |
+| Facts | every element, event, market and operation fact, boxed, the one owner of each, answered through `Element`, `Event`, `Market` and `Operation` like every leaf's; a setter through them states its fact, one [`StatedFacts`](#stated-facts) bit each |
+| Entries | what it states beyond its facts: one ordered run (`row()`) under its protocol's entry root (`root()`, an `Arc<Field>` a codec shares across every message of its dictionary; an empty struct named `entries` where it states none). `record()` is the run as a `FieldRecord`, `entry(name)` one cell by exact name as `Field::index_of` resolves it - null where nothing is stated there, `None` where the root holds no such child - a cell read one buffer read |
+| Setting entries | `set_entries(root, row)` / `try_with_entries` canonicalize once under the root; refused - the message unchanged - where the root is nullable or no struct, names a child as a column the message states itself (a fact column, `stated`, `acknowledgement`, `book`, `instrument`, `children`, `anomalies`, folded) at `$.<name>`, or the row is no run the root accepts; `set_entry(name, value)` replaces one through the child's own value door |
+| Children | the elements it states - a book message's levels - each a `MarketMessage`, one level deep, under one root: `push_child` refuses at `$.children` a child stating children of its own or standing under another root; `children()`, `children_mut()` |
+| Beside the facts | `book()` the book control it states, `is_acknowledgement()` whether it acknowledges another element's step, `instrument()` its [`InstrumentStatement`](#instrument-statement), `anomalies()` the [`Anomaly`](#anomalies) values its reading could not take |
+| Leaves | `into_market_data()`: with children, one leaf per child filed as an order, a quote or an execution - in nondecreasing effective time, stably - each starting from the message's facts and taking every fact the child states, the last child moving the message's facts; without, one leaf of its category with its facts moved and nothing allocated, a full refresh stating the snapshot action one scoped `SnapshotEvent`; an acknowledgement, a book update stating no level, a trade, a batch and any other category none, the first and the last with a deduplicated warning. An execution is one fill: its leaf reads `FILLED` unless canceled. `into_market_leaf()` is the one leaf, refused at `$.children` or `$.marketdatakind` where it is not exactly one |
+| Projection | `MessageIterator::new(messages)` lazily splits messages sorted by time into their leaves, each taking its message's place; a message its intake refused is passed over with a warning, a leaf dated before one already yielded is yielded with a warning, and the source's own failure ends it after every leaf before it, fused |
+| Walk and merge | following and merging are the operation's own over the facts both hold - the entries and children stay the message's own - a merge folding the other statement's anomalies in, each once; `note_conflict` keeps a walk's conflict as an `Anomaly` under `crosscode` |
+| Identity | `finalize` digests its facts, its category, its acknowledgement, its book control, its instrument statement, its entries by name and each child's code - never its anomalies, never its stated bits; `==` and `Hash` read every part, a root by pointer or by value; `stable_hash` is the crate's XXH3-64 over it |
+| Row form | `MarketMessage::field(root, child_root)`: the 6 element, 9 event, 36 market and 5 operation fact columns in `marketdata` order, then `stated` (`uint64`), `acknowledgement`, `book`, `instrument`, the root's children, `children` (a nullable serie of the same form under `child_root`, one level) and `anomalies` (`serie<struct<field: utf8, reason: utf8>>`). `into_scalar()` is one row of it and `from_scalar(root, child_root, row)` restates the message whole - identity included, nothing settled again - refused at `$`, `$.stated`, `$.book.action` or where the entries or a child are. It is no protocol's row - the FIX fixed row is the codec's - but the one pickle and the value stream carry a message by |
+| Size | held inline by `MarketData::Message`, its facts boxed: narrower than the snapshot control, so `MarketData` stays 912 bytes |
+| Bindings | Python `graph.MarketMessage(transunix, kind, *, root=None, row=None, children=None, book=..., **facts)`, frozen and hashable, pickled through its row form, with `record()`, `entry(name)`, `root`, `row`, `children`, `anomalies`, `instrument`, `into_market_data()`, `field`, `into_scalar`, `from_scalar`; JavaScript reads one through `MarketData.asMessage()` - getters only, no constructor and no verb |
+
+=== "Rust"
+
+    ```rust
+    use std::sync::Arc;
+
+    use yggdryl::graph::{BookRef, Element, Event, Market, MarketKind, MarketMessage, MdUpdateAction};
+    use yggdryl::{DataType, Decimal, MarketDataKind, Scalar, Side, StructType};
+
+    // A book message stating its two levels as children.
+    let control = BookRef { action: Some(MdUpdateAction::Snapshot), scope: Some("Symbol=ACME".into()), ..BookRef::default() };
+    let mut book = MarketMessage::new(MarketDataKind::Book);
+    book.set_transunix(1_000);
+    book.set_ticker(Some("ACME".into()), true);
+    book.set_book(Some(control.clone()));
+    for (side, price) in [(Side::Buy, 99), (Side::Sell, 101)] {
+        let mut level = MarketMessage::new(MarketDataKind::Quotation);
+        level.set_side(side, true);
+        level.set_price(Some(Decimal::from_int(price)), true);
+        level.set_book(Some(BookRef { action: Some(MdUpdateAction::New), ..BookRef::default() }));
+        book.push_child(level)?;
+    }
+
+    // Entries: what it states beyond its facts, under one root, read by exact name.
+    let root = Arc::new(
+        DataType::from(StructType::from_fields([DataType::utf8().nullable_field("venue")])?).required_field("entries"),
+    );
+    let book = book.try_with_entries(root, Scalar::from_sequence([Scalar::from("XAMS")]))?;
+    assert_eq!(book.entry("venue").and_then(|cell| cell.as_str().map(str::to_owned)).as_deref(), Some("XAMS"));
+    assert!(book.entry("VENUE").is_none(), "a name is exact");
+
+    // Its row form restates it whole.
+    let row = book.into_scalar();
+    let child_root = Arc::clone(book.children()[0].root());
+    assert_eq!(MarketMessage::from_scalar(Arc::clone(book.root()), Some(child_root), &row)?, book);
+
+    // One leaf per level, what a level states nothing of the message's.
+    let leaves = book.into_market_data();
+    assert_eq!(leaves.len(), 2);
+    assert!(leaves.iter().all(|leaf| leaf.kind() == MarketKind::QuoteEvent && leaf.get_ticker() == Some("ACME")));
+    assert_eq!(leaves[1].get_side(), Side::Sell);
+    ```
