+### Stated facts
+
+`StatedFacts` is the word of the message's source, one bit per fact: a setter through the message's traits marks the fact it names (`PRICE`, `SIDE`, `FILLS` the last quantity, the average price and what traded and is left, `BIDASK` the six facts of the two legs, `LASTPX` the last price and its FX parts, and the rest), a codec's own reading of the wire marks every fact it reads off a field the source stated - never one a derivation filled - and its own word beside them (`set_stated` replaces the word once it has read), and a child's bits say which of its facts lead the message's when it [splits](#the-market-message). `ALL` is every fact; `TRANSUNIX` - a child dated by its own instant - and the two held clocks `HELD_EXECUNIX`, `HELD_SENDUNIX` are outside it. `bits`, `from_bits` (refusing a bit no fact is), `contains`, `intersects`, `union`, `intersection`, `difference`, `insert`, `remove`, `set`.
+
+### Instrument statement
+
+`InstrumentStatement { countrycode, underlyingisin, eusipacode }` is what a message states of its instrument that is a registry fact and no element fact - its country of issue, the instrument it is written on, its EUSIPA product category. A codec sets it at parse - [FIX](../fix/message.md#the-market-message) from `UnderlyingSecurityID(309)`, `UnderlyingSymbol(311)` and the bridge's keys - an [instrument registry](isin-registry.md) learns it through the lifecycle, and it lifts into no column of any leaf.
+
+### Anomalies
+
+`Anomaly { field, reason }`, in `graph::anomaly`, is one thing a message states that its reading could not take as it stands: a value that would not type, an alias stating another value than the field it lost to, an identifier a settle dropped, a walk's conflict under `crosscode`. A message keeps each once, in the order noted, beside its facts and never as one of them - no row holds it and no digest feeds it - and two statements of one message merge them as a union. `Display` is `field: reason`.
+
